-- title:
--   Variable-change homomorphism on the Z-chart of Proj
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a projective Weierstrass cubic over $T$, and $C=(u,r,s,t)$ a Weierstrass variable change over $T$, so that $C\bullet W$ is the transformed cubic. Write $\mathcal A(W)$ for the quotient of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,T$ by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass polynomial of $W$, graded by `projModelGradingCR W`, whose degree-$i$ piece is the image of the degree-$i$ homogeneous submodule. Let $\varphi : \mathcal A(W) \to \mathcal A(C\bullet W)$ be a graded ring homomorphism satisfying: the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source (the hypothesis `hφ` making `Proj.map φ hφ` available), and `IsVariableChangeHom W C φ`, i.e. $\varphi$ fixes the classes of all constants, sends the class of $X_0$ to that of $u^2X_0 + rX_2$, the class of $X_1$ to that of $u^3X_1 + u^2sX_0 + tX_2$, and the class of $X_2$ to that of $X_2$. The assertion is that there is a ring homomorphism $a : \mathrm{ZChartRing}\,W \to \mathrm{ZChartRing}\,(C\bullet W)$ between the degree-zero homogeneous localisations away from the class of $X_2$, such that (i) the chart morphism `zChartι (C • W)` followed by `Proj.map φ hφ` equals `Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom a)` followed by `zChartι W`; (ii) $a$ is compatible with scalars, fixing the image of each $b \in T$ under `fromZeroRingHom` composed with the structure map into the degree-zero part; (iii) $a(X_0/X_2) = u^2\,(X_0/X_2) + r$; and (iv) $a(X_1/X_2) = u^3\,(X_1/X_2) + u^2s\,(X_0/X_2) + t$, the scalars again being inserted through the degree-zero part.
--
--   This is the functoriality of $\mathrm{Proj}$ for a variable change, computed on the affine chart where the third coordinate is invertible: because $\varphi$ fixes the class of $X_2$, the morphism induced on Proj models carries that chart of $C\bullet W$ into the corresponding chart of $W$, and the induced map of chart rings is the classical substitution $x \mapsto u^2x + r$, $y \mapsto u^3y + u^2sx + t$. It is used to recognise a morphism of Proj models as coming from a variable change, notably in identifying isomorphisms of Weierstrass models over Artinian base rings and in showing that a variable change inducing the identity on the Proj model is trivial.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_exists_zChartIota_comp_projMap_eq_specMap_comp_zChartIota_of_isVariableChangeHom.lean

